                "event": "Flash Flood Warning",
                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Wilmington OH",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 20 at 1:54AM EDT until September 20 at 5:00AM EDT by NWS Wilmington OH",
                "description": "FFWILN\n\nThe National Weather Service in Wilmington has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSouthwestern Clinton County in southwestern Ohio...\nSouthern Warren County in southwestern Ohio...\n\n* Until 500 AM EDT.\n\n* At 154 AM EDT, radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy rain\nacross the warned area. Between 2 and 3.5 inches of rain have\nfallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1.5 inches are\npossible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that may experience flash flooding include...\nMason, Lebanon, Monroe, Loveland, Blanchester, Morrow, Kings\nIsland, Highpoint, South Lebanon, Maineville, Clarksville, Midland,\nButlerville, Pleasant Plain, State Route 123 at State Route 132,\nMiddleboro, Fort Ancient, Dallasburg, State Route 350 at US Route\n22 and Murdock.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nTo report flash flooding, go to our website at weather.gov/iln and\nsubmit your report via social media, when you can do so safely.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
                "parameters": {
                    "AWIPSidentifier": [
                        "FFWILN"
                    ],
                    "WMOidentifier": [
                        "WGUS51 KILN 200554"
                    ],
                    "flashFloodDetection": [
                        "RADAR INDICATED"
                    ],
                    "flashFloodDamageThreat": [
                        "CONSIDERABLE"
                    ],
                    "BLOCKCHANNEL": [
                        "EAS",
                        "NWEM"
                    ],
                    "EAS-ORG": [
                        "WXR"
                    ],
                    "VTEC": [
                        "/O.NEW.KILN.FF.W.0092.260920T0554Z-260920T0900Z/"
                    ],
                    "eventEndingTime": [
                        "2026-09-20T05:00:00-04:00"
                    ],
                    "WEAHandling": [
                        "Imminent Threat"
                    ],
                    "CMAMtext": [
                        "NWS: FLASH FLOOD WARNING this area til 5:00 AM EDT. Avoid flooded areas."
                    ],
                    "CMAMlongtext": [
                        "National Weather Service: A FLASH FLOOD WARNING is in effect for this area until 5:00 AM EDT. This is a dangerous and life-threatening situation. Do not attempt to travel unless you are fleeing an area subject to flooding or under an evacuation order."
                    ]
