                "senderName": "NWS Charleston WV",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued September 20 at 12:25AM EDT until September 20 at 3:30AM EDT by NWS Charleston WV",
                "description": "FFWRLX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Charleston has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCentral Athens County in southeastern Ohio...\nNortheastern Vinton County in southeastern Ohio...\n\n* Until 330 AM EDT.\n\n* At 1225 AM EDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 0.5 and 1.5 inches of\nrain have fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are\npossible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nAthens, Nelsonville, Lake Hope State Park, Chauncey, Buchtel,\nAmesville, The Plains and Stroud Run State Park.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe especially cautious at night when it is harder to recognize the\ndangers of flooding.\n\nReport flooding to the National Weather Service by calling toll free,\n800 401 9535, when you can do so safely.",
